        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>By Elena Marchetti · 6 March 2026 · 12 min read</p>",
         "text_color": "#86848c",
         "font_size": "12",
         "line_height": "1.4",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": { "border": { "bottom": 1, "style": "solid", "color": "#ddd8cc" }, "margin_top": 20, "padding_bottom": 22, "margin_bottom": 26 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-hero",
        "type": "workgrid",
        "settings": {
         "columns": 1,
         "items_gap": 0,
         "media_aspect": "16/9",
         "media_tall_aspect": "4/5",
         "media_bg": "#ebe7dd",
         "media_label_color": "#16161a",
         "hover_zoom": false,
         "title_font_family": "heading",
         "title_color": "#16161a",
         "title_size": 20,
         "title_weight": "600",
         "meta_color": "#cf2e2e",
         "meta_size": 11,
         "show_desc": false,
         "desc_color": "#44444c",
         "desc_size": 13,
         "mono_font_family": "Work Sans",
         "items": [
          { "image": "", "media_label": "hero photo — the negotiating room at night", "title": "", "meta": "", "description": "", "link_url": "", "tall": false }
         ]
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-cap",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>The talks ran past midnight three nights in a row before a deal emerged.</p>",
         "text_color": "#86848c",
         "font_size": "12",
         "line_height": "1.5",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 28, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-p1",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>For seventy-two hours, the negotiations looked finished. Aides drifted out of the building, briefings were cancelled, and the wire services began drafting the story of a collapse. Then, sometime after eleven on the third night, a single concession on housing changed everything — and with it, the shape of the coalition.</p>",
         "text_color": "#26262c",
         "font_size": "19",
         "line_height": "1.66",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-p2",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>What follows is a reconstruction, built from conversations with a dozen people in the room, of how a deal that should have been routine came within an hour of falling apart, and what the final compromise will mean for the year ahead.</p>",
         "text_color": "#26262c",
         "font_size": "19",
         "line_height": "1.66",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-bq",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "“Nobody wanted to be the one to walk. So we all stayed, and we all got slightly less than we came for.”",
         "tag": "div",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "24",
         "heading_font_weight": "500",
         "heading_italic": true,
         "heading_color": "#16161a",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": { "border": { "left": 3, "style": "solid", "color": "#cf2e2e" }, "padding_top": 6, "padding_bottom": 6, "padding_left": 26, "margin_top": 30, "margin_bottom": 30 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-h3a",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "The week the maths stopped working",
         "tag": "h3",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "26",
         "heading_font_weight": "600",
         "heading_color": "#16161a",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 34, "margin_bottom": 14 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-p3",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>By Tuesday, the spreadsheet that had anchored every meeting no longer balanced. A late revision to the revenue forecast opened a gap that neither side was willing to close on the other's terms. For two days the conversation circled the same three numbers without landing.</p>",
         "text_color": "#26262c",
         "font_size": "19",
         "line_height": "1.66",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-p4",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>The breakthrough, when it came, was almost accidental — a junior adviser's offhand suggestion that the housing allocation could be phased rather than cut. It was the kind of idea that survives only because everyone is too tired to object.</p>",
         "text_color": "#26262c",
         "font_size": "19",
         "line_height": "1.66",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-h3b",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "What the compromise actually does",
         "tag": "h3",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "26",
         "heading_font_weight": "600",
         "heading_color": "#16161a",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 34, "margin_bottom": 14 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "di-art-p5",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>In practical terms, the deal trades a faster timeline for a smaller first-year commitment. Supporters call it pragmatic; critics call it a delay dressed as a decision. Both are, in their way, correct. The real test arrives next spring, when the phased numbers come due and the easy part is over.</p>",
         "text_color": "#26262c",
         "font_size": "19",
         "line_height": "1.66",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
